<title>FINLAND: Cultor down sharply on profit warning.</title>
<headline>Cultor down sharply on profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish food and biotechnology group Cultor Oy fell sharply on Monday after the company said it warned analysts against overly optimistic result expectations, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1530/1230 GMT, Cultor's usually less liquid 1-series share was down 15 markka or over six percent at 210.00 markka, having earlier touched a low of 201.00 markka. Volume was thin at 6,000 shares with only seven moves.</p>
<p>Cultor's usually more liquid 2-series share was untraded at 236.00 markka.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 80 6805 0247</p>
